  "minimum_forward_operation": [
    "Keep all four inventoried names excluded from borrowed Attach; preserve their UID, ownership and existing workload data. The second tenant namespace has zero PVCs at this observation.",
    "Quiesce Storage entry and positively stop every incompatible old Resource writer/strict reader before the new service serves write intents. Exit/timeout alone is not historical convergence evidence.",
    "After that cutover, create the test PVC through the normal authorized Storage API, with a new unique name and freshly observed UID, Filesystem volume mode, trusted tenant namespace and verified Storage ownership. Freeze that UID via the normal resolver.",
    "Use only this post-cutover new test identity for CP02 initially. The old image digest is now bound through OCI revision f6d7f7b8e90f5def80e937cf2d40780da96f0d50 to the exact UID-precondition implementation. Old workers must still have no chance to select the new object; the binding does not prove that they have exited or that historical requests converged.",
    "Do not import a guessed request as a write_started ticket: recovery would obtain deletion authority over a PVC without a real authorized request. Historical old names remain unqualified unless actual request/identity evidence resolves their state."
  ],
